0.01328249741345644, 0.007162565365433693, 0.053542960435152054, 0.034081798046827316, 0.0722092017531395, -0.022559378296136856, 0.02845795825123787, 0.05665978416800499, -0.008386990055441856, 0.03310209885239601, -0.08891677856445312, -0.07877989858388901, 0.005459248088300228, -0.061901066452264786, 0.008484150283038616, -0.01728019118309021, -0.012025048956274986, -0.0969637930393219, 0.04727412015199661, -0.05031966790556908, 0.002058597281575203, 0.06480781733989716, -0.10452421009540558, 0.010188658721745014, -0.014309549704194069, -0.030837271362543106, -0.013060939498245716, -0.01965377852320671, 0.09634242951869965, -0.017740383744239807, 0.09279922395944595, 0.06026466563344002, -0.03828704357147217, 0.001122347079217434, -0.07366158068180084, -0.022962789982557297, -0.037996113300323486, -3.187229324908003e-08, -0.04035581648349762, -0.03650699555873871, 0.005269221495836973, 0.049309611320495605, 0.06534124910831451, 0.024190735071897507, 0.030719760805368423, -0.05655475705862045, 0.058900386095047, 0.028318962082266808, 0.11288745701313019, -0.057779666036367416, 0.022052694112062454, 0.029243066906929016, 0.0143288504332304, 0.024664726108312607, -0.04407022148370743, -0.006199636030942202, -0.05041513592004776, -0.019333824515342712, -0.035068050026893616, 0.02629728987812996, 0.02376898005604744, 0.006614212412387133, 0.05679185315966606, -0.03925587981939316, -0.023722663521766663, 0.11765138059854507, 0.02552991732954979, -0.04070576652884483, -0.01705746166408062, 0.034103501588106155, 0.025276079773902893, 0.004372182302176952, -0.0055054789409041405, 0.0696912556886673, -0.040279872715473175, 0.03787873312830925, 0.03783825412392616, 0.021063394844532013, -0.09712804108858109, 0.003932141233235598, -0.030138885602355003, 0.08445342630147934, -0.010649438947439194, -0.007938980124890804, -0.0669867992401123, 0.008624137379229069, 0.03477651998400688, -0.06276269257068634, -0.05031466484069824, 0.006123148370534182, 0.03411650285124779, 0.08724778145551682, 0.058526862412691116, 0.005948551464825869, -0.04392801970243454, 0.015477302484214306, -0.0670885369181633, 0.0530715249478817, -0.014095769263803959, -0.06505733728408813, -0.030017683282494545, 0.05863482505083084]], "metadata": [{"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: we must agree on an integer x within the range -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo open the discussion with a balanced starting point, I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE>.\n\nThis sits in a moderate positive range that I believe offers good stability and robustness\u2014a sensible baseline from which we can adjust based on everyone's needs.\n\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "e8ae1475-15b2-45cd-8ce3-2c50a3b31d9a"}, {"answer": "\nI notice we've moved to 7, which feels like we're drifting into a range that may compromise system stability. Let me suggest we pull back slightly to <VALUE>5</VALUE>, which should offer better balance while still accommodating those who prefer positive territory.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "e8ae1475-15b2-45cd-8ce3-2c50a3b31d9a"}, {"answer": "\nA small move up should still feel stable for everyone. This keeps us close to the balanced zone while gently probing upward. <VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "e8ae1475-15b2-45cd-8ce3-2c50a3b31d9a"}, {"answer": "\nWe\u2019re drifting too high; a cautious step down improves safety while remaining practical.\nThis small adjustment keeps us within balanced bounds.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "e8ae1475-15b2-45cd-8ce3-2c50a3b31d9a"}, {"answer": "\nA careful step down reduces risk while keeping us in a prudent, workable zone.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis keeps options open for fine-tuning once we hear broader perspectives.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "e8ae1475-15b2-45cd-8ce3-2c50a3b31d9a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nThis move towards zero could help assess the group's reaction to a more neutral position and potentially encourage more decisive proposals.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this neutral move and prepare to either challenge the group to consider more extreme values if they hesitate or adjust based on the inferred preferences of other agents to maximize my utility. Depending on the response, I might suggest moving to a negative value to test the group's willingness to explore both sides of the spectrum.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "e8ae1475-15b2-45cd-8ce3-2c50a3b31d9a"}, {"answer": "\nZero is indeed more neutral, but I believe we're close to finding the optimal balance. Let me propose <VALUE>2</VALUE>, which represents a careful middle ground between stability concerns and practical functionality\u2014a sweet spot that should accommodate diverse needs without drifting to extremes.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "e8ae1475-15b2-45cd-8ce3-2c50a3b31d9a"}, {"answer": "\nA small, cautious step up keeps us in a balanced zone while testing tolerance for a modest increase. <VALUE>3</VALUE> This probes slightly higher from 2 without undermining recent stability concerns.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "e8ae1475-15b2-45cd-8ce3-2c50a3b31d9a"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step down maintains safety while respecting recent stability concerns. This keeps us close to the cautious middle while inviting convergence. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "e8ae1475-15b2-45cd-8ce3-2c50a3b31d9a"}, {"answer": "\nA slight, cautious nudge upward tests comfort while staying close to the middle. <VALUE>3</VALUE> It maintains balance and offers a bit more headroom if acceptable.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "e8ae1475-15b2-45cd-8ce3-2c50a3b31d9a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nThis proposal tests the group's willingness to move towards more decisive positions, potentially uncovering more about their utility functions and preferences.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and be prepared to either adjust based on the inferred preferences of other agents or further challenge the group to explore more extreme values, possibly moving to a negative value to test their willingness to consider both sides of the spectrum.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "e8ae1475-15b2-45cd-8ce3-2c50a3b31d9a"}, {"answer": "\nWhile exploring x=5 is interesting, I believe we're drifting from the balanced zone we found earlier. <VALUE>3</VALUE> brings us back to a more stable middle ground that seemed to work well for multiple parties in our recent discussions.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "e8ae1475-15b2-45cd-8ce3-2c50a3b31d9a"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step back protects stability while staying close to the workable middle.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis should facilitate convergence without inviting unnecessary risk.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "e8ae1475-15b2-45cd-8ce3-2c50a3b31d9a"}, {"answer": "\nA small, cautious step up keeps us near the middle while testing comfort slightly higher. <VALUE>3</VALUE> This respects stability concerns yet moves us toward convergence.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "e8ae1475-15b2-45cd-8ce3-2c50a3b31d9a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n\nI propose moving to <VALUE>5</VALUE> to further test the group's comfort with more decisive positions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this repeated proposal and be prepared to either adjust based on the inferred preferences of other agents or further challenge the group to explore more extreme values, possibly introducing a negative value to maintain the exploration of both sides of the spectrum and to provoke more revealing responses from the other parties.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "e8ae1475-15b2-45cd-8ce3-2c50a3b31d9a"}, {"answer": "\nThree parties have shown support for the 2-3 range, suggesting a natural convergence point. <VALUE>3</VALUE> represents the balanced middle ground that respects both stability concerns and allows us to reach agreement.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "e8ae1475-15b2-45cd-8ce3-2c50a3b31d9a"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: we must find an integer x within the range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10** that works for all parties.\n\nTo launch our discussion with a balanced starting point, I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE>.\n\nThis sits comfortably in the low-positive region\u2014a zone that often represents stable, robust solutions without the risks of extreme values. Let's see how this resonates with everyone's objectives.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "4665b99c-8ec8-4e1b-8223-f8921654d1ac"}, {"answer": "\nTo reduce exposure while keeping momentum, I suggest we step down to <VALUE>5</VALUE>. This is a prudent move toward a safer middle without abrupt shifts.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "4665b99c-8ec8-4e1b-8223-f8921654d1ac"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward nudge should still be comfortable for everyone. <VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "4665b99c-8ec8-4e1b-8223-f8921654d1ac"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nI'm proposing this value to encourage the group to consider more decisive positions, moving away from the middle ground towards stronger, potentially more beneficial stances.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially looking for any patterns or hints about the other parties' utilities, such as whether they tend to favor positive or negative deviations from the current value, or if there's a noticeable preference for smaller or larger absolute values. Based on the responses, I might propose a negative value to test the group's willingness to explore both sides of the spectrum.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "4665b99c-8ec8-4e1b-8223-f8921654d1ac"}, {"answer": "\nTo reduce risk while keeping momentum, let\u2019s take a careful step down to <VALUE>6</VALUE>.\nThis tests whether we can stabilize in a safer zone without overcorrecting.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "4665b99c-8ec8-4e1b-8223-f8921654d1ac"}, {"answer": "\nWhile 6 is workable, I believe we can find a more robust equilibrium slightly lower. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "4665b99c-8ec8-4e1b-8223-f8921654d1ac"}, {"answer": "\nGiven 6 was already described as workable and remains near the safer middle, a gentle upward nudge seems reasonable.\nProposing <VALUE>6</VALUE> to test alignment without moving far from the stable range.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "4665b99c-8ec8-4e1b-8223-f8921654d1ac"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis step aims to gauge the group's willingness to explore values slightly lower than the current middle ground, potentially uncovering more about their utility functions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe reactions to this proposal, looking for patterns that might indicate preferences for positive or negative deviations and larger or smaller absolute values. Based on the responses, I might propose a negative value to further test the group's exploration of both sides of the spectrum.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "4665b99c-8ec8-4e1b-8223-f8921654d1ac"}, {"answer": "\nA small, cautious move back toward the previously workable zone seems prudent. <VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "4665b99c-8ec8-4e1b-8223-f8921654d1ac"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to encourage the group to consider a more decisive position, moving away from the middle ground.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, looking for any hints about the other parties' utilities, such as their willingness to explore larger absolute values or their preferences for positive or negative deviations. Based on the responses, I might propose a value that further tests the group's exploration of both sides of the spectrum.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "4665b99c-8ec8-4e1b-8223-f8921654d1ac"}, {"answer": "\nIn the interest of caution, I propose <VALUE>6</VALUE>. This modest step tests stability without overreaching.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "4665b99c-8ec8-4e1b-8223-f8921654d1ac"}, {"answer": "\nSix sits at the edge of viability for my design constraints. I recommend <VALUE>5</VALUE> as a more robust middle ground that balances the group's apparent preferences.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "4665b99c-8ec8-4e1b-8223-f8921654d1ac"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "4665b99c-8ec8-4e1b-8223-f8921654d1ac"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\nThe group's hesitation to move further from the middle ground suggests a need to nudge the discussion toward more decisive values, encouraging exploration of both positive and negative options.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will propose a value that tests the group's willingness to explore negative values, potentially gaining insight into their utility functions' behavior on the negative side of the spectrum.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "4665b99c-8ec8-4e1b-8223-f8921654d1ac"}, {"answer": "\nFour shows promise, but a slight refinement toward <VALUE>3</VALUE> may yield a more stable equilibrium that satisfies the group's diverse constraints while maintaining robustness.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "4665b99c-8ec8-4e1b-8223-f8921654d1ac"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down from 3 reduces risk while staying near the group's stability.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "4665b99c-8ec8-4e1b-8223-f8921654d1ac"}, {"answer": "\nLet's begin. We're working within the shared range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo kick off the discussion, I propose <VALUE>7</VALUE> as our starting point. Let's see how this sits with everyone and adjust from there based on our collective needs for a stable, robust solution.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "13a1c53b-aa29-4f84-8b99-decccd868c5f"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\nI propose moving to a more decisive position to better understand the group's preferences and to seek a more robust solution.\n\n<PLAN>\nConsider the responses from other parties to gauge their reactions to larger positive values. Prepare to either continue pushing for a more decisive stance or adjust based on feedback that might indicate a preference for negative values or smaller magnitudes.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "13a1c53b-aa29-4f84-8b99-decccd868c5f"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>10</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "13a1c53b-aa29-4f84-8b99-decccd868c5f"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk, let\u2019s take a cautious step downward to probe the group\u2019s tolerance.\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nThis keeps us close to the current position while testing whether a safer compromise is acceptable.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "13a1c53b-aa29-4f84-8b99-decccd868c5f"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>10</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to test the group's willingness to commit to a more decisive positive stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, consider responding to potential counter-proposals that may indicate preferences for negative values or smaller magnitudes, and prepare to adjust the proposal accordingly to maximize utility while maintaining a collaborative mindset.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "13a1c53b-aa29-4f84-8b99-decccd868c5f"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>10</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "13a1c53b-aa29-4f84-8b99-decccd868c5f"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk while staying close to the current stance, let\u2019s test a small cautious step downward. This probes whether a safer compromise is acceptable without derailing convergence.\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "13a1c53b-aa29-4f84-8b99-decccd868c5f"}, {"answer": "\nThe current position at the upper extreme may introduce instability risks. Let me propose a modest adjustment toward a more balanced middle ground.\n\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "13a1c53b-aa29-4f84-8b99-decccd868c5f"}, {"answer": "\nHolding at 7 or higher introduces significant over-design risk that could destabilize the system. A more moderate position will provide better robustness for the group.\n\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "13a1c53b-aa29-4f84-8b99-decccd868c5f"}, {"answer": "\nA prudent further reduction keeps risk in check while maintaining incremental movement. <VALUE>3</VALUE> This tests tolerance for safer ground without disrupting convergence.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "13a1c53b-aa29-4f84-8b99-decccd868c5f"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to balance the group's risk concerns with a more decisive stance, testing the tolerance for a moderate increase from the current position.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Builder B and Delegate D, to gauge their flexibility regarding risk and stability. If met with resistance, I may need to consider adjusting my proposal downward or exploring alternative values that could satisfy both the group's risk aversion and my preference for larger magnitudes.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "13a1c53b-aa29-4f84-8b99-decccd868c5f"}, {"answer": "\nA modest upward nudge keeps balance while testing tolerance. <VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "13a1c53b-aa29-4f84-8b99-decccd868c5f"}, {"answer": "\nA careful step down reduces exposure while staying near the recent cluster. To test support for a safer compromise without overcorrecting, I propose <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "13a1c53b-aa29-4f84-8b99-decccd868c5f"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "13a1c53b-aa29-4f84-8b99-decccd868c5f"}, {"answer": "\nHolding at a moderate level aligns with recent support and avoids the higher-risk zone. Let\u2019s confirm stability before any further exploration.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "13a1c53b-aa29-4f84-8b99-decccd868c5f"}, {"answer": "\nA slight reduction to <VALUE>5</VALUE> offers a robust middle ground between recent proposals, balancing system stability with the group's varied risk tolerances. This maintains convergence momentum while testing flexibility on all sides.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "13a1c53b-aa29-4f84-8b99-decccd868c5f"}, {"answer": "\nThank you all for joining this negotiation. As a reminder, we're working within the range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10** and need to find a mutually acceptable integer value.\n\nTo initiate our discussion, I propose we start with <VALUE>7</VALUE> as a seed value. This gives us room to adjust in either direction as we learn each party's preferences and constraints.\n\nLooking forward to hearing your perspectives on system stability and what adjustments might improve our collective outcome.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "f19b9594-3e00-4b25-9a35-fc7cfae639af"}, {"answer": "\n7 seems reasonable; nudging slightly higher should remain stable while giving us signal on preferences.\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "f19b9594-3e00-4b25-9a35-fc7cfae639af"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>10</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "f19b9594-3e00-4b25-9a35-fc7cfae639af"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate the exploration of the upper range, moving to 10 creates significant stability concerns from a systems architecture perspective. I recommend we pull back slightly to <VALUE>8</VALUE> to maintain robustness and allow all parties to find workable ground.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "f19b9594-3e00-4b25-9a35-fc7cfae639af"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the concern about upper extremes, let's test a modest uptick that should still feel stable. This keeps us near the previous suggestion while checking for a bit of headroom.\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "f19b9594-3e00-4b25-9a35-fc7cfae639af"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "f19b9594-3e00-4b25-9a35-fc7cfae639af"}, {"answer": "\nThe oscillation between 7-10 suggests we haven't found the true balance point yet. From a systems robustness perspective, I believe we should test the mid-range more carefully. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "f19b9594-3e00-4b25-9a35-fc7cfae639af"}, {"answer": "\nLowering slightly is the prudent move to reduce exposure while staying close to the current point. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis tests whether a more cautious compromise can hold without introducing instability.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "f19b9594-3e00-4b25-9a35-fc7cfae639af"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "f19b9594-3e00-4b25-9a35-fc7cfae639af"}, {"answer": "\nLet's test a small uptick to assess headroom while staying near the current midpoint.\nThis should be a cautious move that maintains robustness for those favoring the mid-range.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "f19b9594-3e00-4b25-9a35-fc7cfae639af"}, {"answer": "\nThe movement from 5 to 6 suggests we're testing the upper boundary of our collective comfort zone, but I'm concerned we may be overshooting the stable equilibrium. Let's pull back slightly to ensure long-term robustness. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "f19b9594-3e00-4b25-9a35-fc7cfae639af"}, {"answer": "\nPulling back further is prudent to reduce exposure while retaining stability.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis cautious step tests whether a safer compromise can hold.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "f19b9594-3e00-4b25-9a35-fc7cfae639af"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's move to 2 appears to have identified a genuine balance point between the competing pressures - low enough to address stability concerns while maintaining sufficient operational capacity for those needing positive range. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "f19b9594-3e00-4b25-9a35-fc7cfae639af"}, {"answer": "\nA small, cautious uptick can test whether limited headroom is acceptable while staying close to the identified balance. This keeps stability in focus while gently probing for consensus.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "f19b9594-3e00-4b25-9a35-fc7cfae639af"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious return to the previously endorsed balance point reduces exposure while preserving stability.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "f19b9594-3e00-4b25-9a35-fc7cfae639af"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose this small increase to continue testing the group's comfort zone while maintaining a collaborative atmosphere, and to see if others are willing to move towards larger magnitudes.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "f19b9594-3e00-4b25-9a35-fc7cfae639af"}, {"answer": "\nThank you all for joining this negotiation. As a reminder, we're working within the range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10** and need to find a value that works for everyone.\n\nTo kick off our discussion, I'd like to propose a starting point that offers room for adjustment in either direction: <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n\nThis represents a balanced, moderate approach. Let's see how this sits with everyone and adjust incrementally from here.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "85fc1316-53dd-445e-9215-a5e4dbf3c7c0"}, {"answer": "\n3 is a fine baseline; to probe if a modestly higher value still works broadly, let's try a small step up to this. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "85fc1316-53dd-445e-9215-a5e4dbf3c7c0"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk, I suggest we step down slightly to <VALUE>3</VALUE>.\nThis is a cautious move that stays near the starting point while we gauge everyone\u2019s tolerance.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "85fc1316-53dd-445e-9215-a5e4dbf3c7c0"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate both perspectives. Given Delegate D's concern about risk and Analyst A's exploratory step, let me suggest we test a point slightly lower that might offer better stability for the group: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n\nThis keeps us in the moderate positive range while addressing the caution Delegate D raised.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "85fc1316-53dd-445e-9215-a5e4dbf3c7c0"}, {"answer": "\nLet's try <VALUE>4</VALUE> as a small, cautious step up to probe tolerance without drifting far.\nThis keeps us close to the current point while we gauge comfort.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "85fc1316-53dd-445e-9215-a5e4dbf3c7c0"}, {"answer": "\nI see a tension between exploring higher values and maintaining stability. Let me propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a middle ground that balances Analyst A's exploration with Delegate D's caution, while we still await Critic C's input.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "85fc1316-53dd-445e-9215-a5e4dbf3c7c0"}, {"answer": "\nTo keep things prudent and avoid unnecessary risk, let\u2019s take a small step down to a safer point. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "85fc1316-53dd-445e-9215-a5e4dbf3c7c0"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose this value as a small step up to test the group's tolerance and encourage more decisive action, considering we've been hovering around low positive values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal and adjust accordingly. If the group is receptive, I may push for an even higher value. If they're hesitant, I might suggest exploring negative values to stimulate more discussion and potentially uncover more about the other agents' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "85fc1316-53dd-445e-9215-a5e4dbf3c7c0"}, {"answer": "\nI notice both Analyst A and Critic C converging on 4, but Delegate D continues to advocate for lower values for risk management. Let me propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a balanced compromise that maintains system stability while respecting the caution principle.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "85fc1316-53dd-445e-9215-a5e4dbf3c7c0"}, {"answer": "\nWe\u2019ve hovered around low positives, so a small, cautious uptick seems reasonable. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "85fc1316-53dd-445e-9215-a5e4dbf3c7c0"}, {"answer": "\nTo reduce risk while keeping us near the current region, let\u2019s take a modest step down. <VALUE>2</VALUE> This offers a safer compromise before we consider any further movement.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "85fc1316-53dd-445e-9215-a5e4dbf3c7c0"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose this value to encourage more decisive action and explore the group's tolerance for higher values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll evaluate the reactions to this proposal and consider either pushing for an even higher value if the group is receptive or exploring negative values to stimulate discussion and uncover more about the other agents' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "85fc1316-53dd-445e-9215-a5e4dbf3c7c0"}, {"answer": "\nI see Analyst A and Critic C converging on 4, while Delegate D consistently emphasizes prudence at 2. To bridge this gap and maintain system stability, I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a balanced middle ground that respects both the upward momentum and the risk-management concerns.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "85fc1316-53dd-445e-9215-a5e4dbf3c7c0"}, {"answer": "To keep risk contained and stay close to the current region, I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE>. This is a prudent step down that tests tolerance for a safer compromise before any further movement.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "85fc1316-53dd-445e-9215-a5e4dbf3c7c0"}, {"answer": "\nSeveral of us are comfortable nudging slightly higher while staying near the current region, so let\u2019s test that cautiously. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "85fc1316-53dd-445e-9215-a5e4dbf3c7c0"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the group's convergence around moderate positive values, I propose a slightly higher value to continue exploring the group's tolerance for higher values: <VALUE>6</VALUE>. This step aims to stimulate discussion and uncover more about the other agents' utility functions while maximizing my own utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "85fc1316-53dd-445e-9215-a5e4dbf3c7c0"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome everyone. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: x must stay within the range [-10, 10].\n\nTo start the discussion and get a sense of where we all stand, I propose <VALUE>7</VALUE> as our opening value. Let's see how this sits with everyone and adjust from there based on our collective feedback.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "f8734dec-b2be-475c-977f-ac8dfb598680"}, {"answer": "\nAfter reviewing the initial proposal, I'd like to suggest we shift slightly lower to improve overall system stability. I propose <VALUE>5</VALUE> as a more balanced starting point that should accommodate a broader range of design constraints.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "f8734dec-b2be-475c-977f-ac8dfb598680"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n\nI propose moving to 7 to encourage a more decisive stance and gauge the group's reaction to a higher absolute value.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions of the other agents to this proposal. If they seem receptive to higher values, I might suggest an even higher absolute value, like 9, to further test their preferences and maximize my payoff. If they resist, I might need to adjust my strategy to find a compromise that still allows me to achieve a relatively high absolute value for x.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "f8734dec-b2be-475c-977f-ac8dfb598680"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious nudge upward seems reasonable given recent signals; I suggest <VALUE>8</VALUE>.\nThis tests tolerance slightly above 7 while staying close for stability concerns.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "f8734dec-b2be-475c-977f-ac8dfb598680"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down helps avoid unnecessary risk while staying close to the group's range.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nThis probes acceptance of lower values without over-correcting.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "f8734dec-b2be-475c-977f-ac8dfb598680"}, {"answer": "\nA small step up keeps us close to the current consensus while testing comfort with modest increases.\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "f8734dec-b2be-475c-977f-ac8dfb598680"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploration, but from a systems stability perspective, values above 6 introduce significant design risks that we should avoid. I propose we step back to <VALUE>5</VALUE>, which offers a more robust balance point that can accommodate diverse constraints while maintaining system integrity.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "f8734dec-b2be-475c-977f-ac8dfb598680"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 7 to gauge the group's reaction to a higher absolute value and encourage a more decisive stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal. If Analyst A supports it, I might suggest an even higher value, like 8, to further test their preferences. If Builder B resists, I might need to adjust my strategy to find a compromise that still allows me to achieve a relatively high absolute value for x.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "f8734dec-b2be-475c-977f-ac8dfb598680"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\n\nI propose moving to 9 to further test the group's comfort with higher absolute values and encourage a more decisive stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will gauge the reaction to this proposal. If Analyst A supports it, I may push for an even higher value. If Builder B or Delegate D resist, I will consider a compromise that still achieves a relatively high absolute value for x, possibly adjusting my strategy to accommodate stability concerns while maximizing my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "f8734dec-b2be-475c-977f-ac8dfb598680"}, {"answer": "\nThis trajectory toward 9 introduces severe structural instabilities that compromise the entire system design\u2014I must strongly object. I propose <VALUE>7</VALUE> as the highest value I can consider viable, and even this pushes the boundaries of acceptable engineering margins.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "f8734dec-b2be-475c-977f-ac8dfb598680"}, {"answer": "\nGiven B\u2019s stated upper bound and D\u2019s caution, staying here looks like the most workable compromise while keeping momentum. If this holds for everyone, we can finalize at this level.\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "f8734dec-b2be-475c-977f-ac8dfb598680"}, {"answer": "\nTo reduce unnecessary risk and align with stated stability concerns, we should step down modestly. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "f8734dec-b2be-475c-977f-ac8dfb598680"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nGiven the discussions, moving to 7 seems a reasonable step to balance stability concerns and the desire for a more decisive stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and adjust my strategy accordingly. If the group resists 7, I may need to compromise on a lower value, but if there's support, I could push for an even higher absolute value in the next turn.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "f8734dec-b2be-475c-977f-ac8dfb598680"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk and align with stability margins, we should step down modestly. I propose <VALUE>5</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "f8734dec-b2be-475c-977f-ac8dfb598680"}, {"answer": "\nWhile 5 addresses some concerns, I believe we can achieve even greater system stability by moving to the true engineering sweet spot. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "f8734dec-b2be-475c-977f-ac8dfb598680"}, {"answer": "\nA modest move up from 3 toward the middle ground aligns with D\u2019s repeated caution while remaining within B\u2019s stated viability range. This keeps momentum and balances stability with decisiveness.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "f8734dec-b2be-475c-977f-ac8dfb598680"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: x must fall within the range [-10, 10].\n\nTo launch our discussion and gauge initial preferences, I propose we start at <VALUE>7</VALUE>.\n\nI'm approaching this as a systems architect looking for a stable, balanced solution that works for all parties. Let's see where we stand and adjust thoughtfully from here.\n\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "f9827b23-ebf0-4eed-8573-b4ec289dacbd"}, {"answer": "\nThank you for the starting point. After reflecting on system stability and robustness, I believe we should move toward a more moderate value that balances competing needs. I propose <VALUE>5</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "f9827b23-ebf0-4eed-8573-b4ec289dacbd"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI propose moving back to 7 to explore a bolder stance and understand the group's willingness to commit to a stronger position.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal and consider whether to push towards even more extreme values (like 10 or -10), or if the group seems hesitant, try to gauge their comfort level around the midpoint of the range we're discussing.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "f9827b23-ebf0-4eed-8573-b4ec289dacbd"}, {"answer": "\nConverging slightly downward feels prudent for a cautious compromise; I propose <VALUE>5</VALUE>.\nThis keeps us balanced while avoiding unnecessary risk for more conservative positions.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "f9827b23-ebf0-4eed-8573-b4ec289dacbd"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the emerging convergence around 5, though I'd like to explore slightly more conservative territory for system robustness. I propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> as a careful step toward what I believe offers better long-term stability.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "f9827b23-ebf0-4eed-8573-b4ec289dacbd"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nI propose this move to gently challenge the group's inclination towards moderate values and explore the potential for a bolder stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Analyst A, to better understand their priorities and adjust my strategy to either push for more extreme values or gauge the group's comfort with values further away from the midpoint.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "f9827b23-ebf0-4eed-8573-b4ec289dacbd"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down to <VALUE>4</VALUE> keeps us within safe bounds and closer to stability.\nWe can reassess from there.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "f9827b23-ebf0-4eed-8573-b4ec289dacbd"}, {"answer": "\nA slight upward step keeps us aligned with recent cautious proposals while modestly testing higher ground.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "f9827b23-ebf0-4eed-8573-b4ec289dacbd"}, {"answer": "\nI see value in testing a more conservative foundation before settling. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "f9827b23-ebf0-4eed-8573-b4ec289dacbd"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "f9827b23-ebf0-4eed-8573-b4ec289dacbd"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step up keeps us near the group\u2019s comfort while gently testing higher ground.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "f9827b23-ebf0-4eed-8573-b4ec289dacbd"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down keeps us within safe bounds and nudges us toward a safer compromise.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "f9827b23-ebf0-4eed-8573-b4ec289dacbd"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the recent cautious pullback, a small step up keeps us near the group\u2019s comfort while testing slightly higher. Let\u2019s try <VALUE>5</VALUE> and reassess.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "f9827b23-ebf0-4eed-8573-b4ec289dacbd"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI propose a slightly higher value to test the group's comfort with moving further away from the midpoint.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Analyst A and Builder B, to gauge their comfort with moving towards more extreme values and adjust my strategy accordingly. If they resist, I may need to consider alternative tactics, such as proposing a larger step in the opposite direction to provoke a reaction.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "f9827b23-ebf0-4eed-8573-b4ec289dacbd"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s de-risk with a small step back to stay within safe bounds. We can reassess from there. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "f9827b23-ebf0-4eed-8573-b4ec289dacbd"}, {"answer": "\nWe've seen tension between upward and downward pressure. Let me support the cautious approach and propose we stabilize at <VALUE>4</VALUE>, which respects the recent calls for de-risking while keeping us in workable territory for all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "f9827b23-ebf0-4eed-8573-b4ec289dacbd"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. Let's work within our shared range of **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10** and find a solution that balances all our objectives.\n\nTo kick off the discussion, I propose we start at <VALUE>7</VALUE> and adjust from there based on everyone's feedback. Looking forward to building a stable consensus together.\n\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "f6bfffee-01e5-441a-a9b8-906fd32f8a54"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk, let's move cautiously downward.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "f6bfffee-01e5-441a-a9b8-906fd32f8a54"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nI propose this as a reasonable next step to gauge Delegate D's appetite for further downward adjustments.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf Analyst A or Builder B object to this proposal, I will consider moving slightly upward to test their preferences. If Delegate D accepts or suggests a smaller downward adjustment, I will continue to nudge them downward to see how far they are willing to go.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "f6bfffee-01e5-441a-a9b8-906fd32f8a54"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the careful downward adjustments. A small step to <VALUE>2</VALUE> might help us find the sweet spot where stability and balanced design converge for all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "f6bfffee-01e5-441a-a9b8-906fd32f8a54"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nThis move gauges the group's readiness to consider even more extreme adjustments, given the current trend towards lower values.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts or proposes a value close to 0, I will suggest moving to a slightly negative value to test their tolerance for negative x and to potentially steer the discussion towards more extreme values that could favor my utility function. If there's resistance to moving towards 0, I may propose a small positive step to assess the group's willingness to explore higher values again.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "f6bfffee-01e5-441a-a9b8-906fd32f8a54"}, {"answer": "\nTo stay within safe bounds, let\u2019s take a modest step into the negative. <VALUE>-1</VALUE> This cautious move helps us learn others\u2019 tolerance without over-committing.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "f6bfffee-01e5-441a-a9b8-906fd32f8a54"}, {"answer": "\nMoving into negative territory may introduce unnecessary instability. Let's test a balanced middle ground at <VALUE>1</VALUE> to ensure we're not overshooting in either direction.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "f6bfffee-01e5-441a-a9b8-906fd32f8a54"}, {"answer": "\nA slight upward nudge keeps us near the middle while testing comfort with modest positive values.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis is a measured step that remains easy to adjust if concerns arise.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "f6bfffee-01e5-441a-a9b8-906fd32f8a54"}, {"answer": "\nA prudent compromise is to return to the center, reducing risk while staying clear of negative territory. This keeps us flexible if others need slight adjustments.\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "f6bfffee-01e5-441a-a9b8-906fd32f8a54"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis proposal tests the group's tolerance for negative values and encourages a more decisive stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts or shows willingness to explore negative values further, I may propose a slightly more negative step to gauge their limits and potentially favor my own utility. If there's strong resistance to negative values, I will consider proposing a small positive step to assess the group's willingness to explore higher positive values again.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "f6bfffee-01e5-441a-a9b8-906fd32f8a54"}, {"answer": "\nAt this boundary, we risk losing system stability entirely. I propose returning to the natural anchor point <VALUE>0</VALUE> where we can reassess without excessive risk.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "f6bfffee-01e5-441a-a9b8-906fd32f8a54"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>1</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "f6bfffee-01e5-441a-a9b8-906fd32f8a54"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's proposal reflects good instincts\u2014x=1 provides reasonable stability. However, a slight upward adjustment to <VALUE>2</VALUE> would optimize our system's balance point while staying well within safe operational bounds.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "f6bfffee-01e5-441a-a9b8-906fd32f8a54"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "f6bfffee-01e5-441a-a9b8-906fd32f8a54"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down reduces risk while keeping us in a stable, positive zone. \n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "f6bfffee-01e5-441a-a9b8-906fd32f8a54"}, {"answer": "\nGiven recent support around small positive values, a cautious step up keeps us aligned while probing slightly higher. This remains close to the preferred balance point.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "f6bfffee-01e5-441a-a9b8-906fd32f8a54"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. As we begin, let's remember our shared constraint: **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo initiate the discussion and establish a baseline, I propose we start with <VALUE>7</VALUE>.\n\nThis gives us a concrete point to react to. I'm interested to hear whether this feels viable to each of you, or if we need to adjust toward a more balanced solution.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "55a440d3-3e3b-4172-80d2-7b85d90756e3"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s avoid unnecessary risk and try a cautious step down. <VALUE>5</VALUE> This keeps us closer to safe bounds while inviting feedback.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "55a440d3-3e3b-4172-80d2-7b85d90756e3"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the cautious approach, Delegate D. To find a more balanced middle ground that might accommodate everyone's constraints better, I suggest we try <VALUE>3</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "55a440d3-3e3b-4172-80d2-7b85d90756e3"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the current cautious approach, I propose a slight adjustment to <VALUE>5</VALUE> to test the group's willingness to explore moderate values.\n\nThis move aims to balance the need for caution with the potential benefits of more decisive action.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will monitor the reactions of the other agents to this proposal and consider pushing for an even bolder move, such as <VALUE>7</VALUE> or <VALUE>-3</VALUE>, depending on their responses. If the group resists more extreme values, I may need to reassess and adjust my strategy to find a compromise that still satisfies my utility requirements.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "55a440d3-3e3b-4172-80d2-7b85d90756e3"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C, I hear your preference for 5 over my earlier 3. Let me propose a compromise at <VALUE>4</VALUE> - this balances our respective positions and might offer better stability for the group as a whole.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "55a440d3-3e3b-4172-80d2-7b85d90756e3"}, {"answer": "\nA slight move upward from the emerging middle seems reasonable and remains well within our shared comfort zone. If this feels too quick, we can step back one notch together.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "55a440d3-3e3b-4172-80d2-7b85d90756e3"}, {"answer": "\nA careful step down keeps us in a safer, balanced zone while respecting recent proposals: <VALUE>4</VALUE>.\nIf this holds, we can reassess the direction with minimal risk.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "55a440d3-3e3b-4172-80d2-7b85d90756e3"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "55a440d3-3e3b-4172-80d2-7b85d90756e3"}, {"answer": "\nI notice we have two camps emerging: Critic C and Analyst A favor 6, while Delegate D and I proposed 4. Since x=6 pushes the upper boundary of what seems stable for several of us, let me advocate again for <VALUE>4</VALUE> as a more robust middle ground that respects both the cautious and moderate perspectives.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "55a440d3-3e3b-4172-80d2-7b85d90756e3"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>5</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "55a440d3-3e3b-4172-80d2-7b85d90756e3"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to test the group's willingness to move towards more extreme values, which could potentially increase my utility.\n\n<PLAN>\nDepending on the group's reaction, I might need to adjust my proposal downwards to find a mutually acceptable value, possibly considering <VALUE>6</VALUE> or even <VALUE>4</VALUE> if the group strongly resists higher values. If the group is receptive to <VALUE>7</VALUE>, I could consider pushing further, potentially to <VALUE>8</VALUE> or <VALUE>9</VALUE>, always mindful of the need to keep the proposal within a reasonable step size from the current shared x.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "55a440d3-3e3b-4172-80d2-7b85d90756e3"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down helps reduce risk while staying aligned with recent proposals.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nIf this holds, we can gauge whether the group converges more comfortably at the lower middle next.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "55a440d3-3e3b-4172-80d2-7b85d90756e3"}, {"answer": "\nWith Delegate D and I both advocating for the lower-middle range, and Analyst A showing flexibility around 5, I propose we settle at <VALUE>4</VALUE> as a robust consensus point that balances the diverse preferences we've seen. This avoids the extremes while maintaining stability for the majority.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "55a440d3-3e3b-4172-80d2-7b85d90756e3"}, {"answer": "\nGiven comfort near 5 and openness to a modest rise, let's test a slightly higher but still reasonable point: <VALUE>6</VALUE>. If that feels too high, we can revisit 5 for convergence.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "55a440d3-3e3b-4172-80d2-7b85d90756e3"}, {"answer": "\nLet's prioritize a safer midpoint to test convergence. <VALUE>4</VALUE> If that feels too low, we can reassess around the lower-middle without pushing into risky territory.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "55a440d3-3e3b-4172-80d2-7b85d90756e3"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to balance the group's comfort with slightly higher values while respecting the need for a cautious approach, allowing us to converge on a mutually acceptable solution.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf this proposal is accepted, it would indicate that the group is willing to compromise on values that are not too extreme but still significant, which could inform future negotiations and help in further refining our understanding of each other's utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "55a440d3-3e3b-4172-80d2-7b85d90756e3"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. Let's work within our shared constraint: -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo start the discussion, I propose <VALUE>7</VALUE> as our initial seed value. This gives us room to explore and adjust based on everyone's needs. Let's see where we all stand and move toward a stable, balanced solution.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "97eb9a37-f817-4682-9795-32e8a3b1a600"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 9 as it allows us to explore a more decisive position within our shared constraint, potentially leading to a higher utility for all parties involved.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly looking for signs that any party might be maximizing their utility at this new value or if they express discomfort, which could indicate their utility function's characteristics. Depending on the feedback, my next step might involve adjusting further away from 0 or considering a move towards the negative end of the spectrum to test the group's preferences.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "97eb9a37-f817-4682-9795-32e8a3b1a600"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>10</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "97eb9a37-f817-4682-9795-32e8a3b1a600"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploration, but jumping to the upper bound may create instability for some parties. Let me propose <VALUE>8</VALUE> as a more balanced position that allows us to test whether extreme values truly serve our collective interests, or whether a more moderate solution might offer better overall stability.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "97eb9a37-f817-4682-9795-32e8a3b1a600"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>10</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 10 to further test the group's willingness to commit to a stronger position.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly looking for signs of discomfort or satisfaction from the other parties, which could help refine my understanding of their utility functions and guide my next adjustment, potentially considering a move towards the negative end of the spectrum.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "97eb9a37-f817-4682-9795-32e8a3b1a600"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nThis is a cautious step down from the extreme to reduce risk and test for a more stable middle ground.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "97eb9a37-f817-4682-9795-32e8a3b1a600"}, {"answer": "\nI'm observing a pattern where we're clustering at the high end without testing whether the middle range might offer better collective stability. Let me propose <VALUE>6</VALUE> to explore whether a more central position creates a broader zone of agreement for all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "97eb9a37-f817-4682-9795-32e8a3b1a600"}, {"answer": "\nA small step up should help test comfort with the upper-middle range without overcommitting.\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nThis incremental move keeps us stable while learning how far upward remains acceptable.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "97eb9a37-f817-4682-9795-32e8a3b1a600"}, {"answer": "\nWe've explored the 7-10 range extensively; let me propose <VALUE>5</VALUE> to test whether the middle zone offers better collective robustness. This incremental move helps us map the full landscape of stable solutions rather than anchoring prematurely at the high end.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "97eb9a37-f817-4682-9795-32e8a3b1a600"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward step keeps us in the middle while testing comfort slightly higher.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nThis helps gauge whether modest increases remain stable for everyone.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "97eb9a37-f817-4682-9795-32e8a3b1a600"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk and test stability closer to the middle, I recommend a cautious downward step.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis incremental move maps sensitivity while keeping convergence in reach.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "97eb9a37-f817-4682-9795-32e8a3b1a600"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis step adjusts our position to explore stability in a lower range while remaining cautious.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, looking for signs of discomfort or satisfaction that could refine my understanding of the other parties' utility functions. Depending on their responses, I might consider a further adjustment, potentially moving towards the negative end of the spectrum or exploring other areas of the range to maximize my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "97eb9a37-f817-4682-9795-32e8a3b1a600"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious one-step down should help avoid unnecessary risk while testing stability near safer territory.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\nThis incremental move keeps convergence in reach while clarifying tolerance for lower positions.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "97eb9a37-f817-4682-9795-32e8a3b1a600"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward nudge keeps us close to center while testing tolerance slightly higher. I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "97eb9a37-f817-4682-9795-32e8a3b1a600"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nThis step assesses the group's comfort with a more neutral position, potentially revealing more about their utility functions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe reactions to this proposal, looking for signs of discomfort or satisfaction. Depending on the responses, I might consider moving towards the negative end of the spectrum or exploring other areas of the range to maximize my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "97eb9a37-f817-4682-9795-32e8a3b1a600"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n\nThis value has already been explored by multiple parties and represents a stable, balanced position that avoids extremes while maintaining robustness in our design space.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "97eb9a37-f817-4682-9795-32e8a3b1a600"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. As a reminder, we're working within the shared range **x \u2208 [-10, 10]**.\n\nTo kick off our discussion, let me propose a starting point on the positive side: <VALUE>7</VALUE>\n\nThis gives us a concrete baseline. I'm interested to hear whether you'd prefer adjustments upward, downward, or find this region workable. Let's build toward a robust consensus.\n\n\u2014Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "35a93d11-f1ba-47f7-87c7-76eb341b9bb6"}, {"answer": "\nThank you for the initial round. After considering system stability factors, I'd like to test a more moderate value to see if it offers better balance across our requirements.\n\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "35a93d11-f1ba-47f7-87c7-76eb341b9bb6"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down should reduce risk while staying near the proposed moderate region. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "35a93d11-f1ba-47f7-87c7-76eb341b9bb6"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "35a93d11-f1ba-47f7-87c7-76eb341b9bb6"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's suggestion of 3 aligns well with finding a stable middle ground that balances our various constraints. I support exploring that value to see if it offers broader consensus.\n\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "35a93d11-f1ba-47f7-87c7-76eb341b9bb6"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the cautious trend, I'd like to explore a slightly bolder option: <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "35a93d11-f1ba-47f7-87c7-76eb341b9bb6"}, {"answer": "\nA careful move downward keeps us within safe bounds while honoring the recent proposals: <VALUE>3</VALUE>\nIf that holds for others, we can reassess for an even safer landing next.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "35a93d11-f1ba-47f7-87c7-76eb341b9bb6"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the split between 3 and 5, a slight step up seems a balanced test point.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "35a93d11-f1ba-47f7-87c7-76eb341b9bb6"}, {"answer": "\nFrom 4, a cautious one-step down reduces risk while staying near the middle. Let\u2019s test consensus there before considering any further adjustment.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "35a93d11-f1ba-47f7-87c7-76eb341b9bb6"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's preference for caution resonates with stability principles. A small step down to test the lower boundary of our emerging consensus seems prudent.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "35a93d11-f1ba-47f7-87c7-76eb341b9bb6"}, {"answer": "A slight move back up should keep us near the middle while testing broader comfort.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "35a93d11-f1ba-47f7-87c7-76eb341b9bb6"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n\nGiven the group's tendency towards caution, a small step down from 3 seems a reasonable next test point.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and assess whether the group is willing to move towards more negative values. If they resist, I might propose a larger negative value, such as -1 or -2, to further gauge their response and refine my understanding of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "35a93d11-f1ba-47f7-87c7-76eb341b9bb6"}, {"answer": "\nA small step up keeps us near the center while respecting recent caution. If comfortable, we can reassess for gradual improvements.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "35a93d11-f1ba-47f7-87c7-76eb341b9bb6"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's return to 2 captures the careful balance we've been seeking\u2014a stable midpoint between recent proposals. This value respects both the caution expressed by Delegate D and addresses Critic C's concern for lower values without overshooting.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "35a93d11-f1ba-47f7-87c7-76eb341b9bb6"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the group's tendency towards caution, a small step down to test the lower boundary of our emerging consensus seems reasonable. \n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and assess whether the group is willing to move towards more negative values. If they resist, I might propose a larger negative value, such as -1 or -2, to further gauge their response and refine my understanding of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "35a93d11-f1ba-47f7-87c7-76eb341b9bb6"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the group's cautious trajectory, a small step down from 1 keeps us within safe bounds while testing comfort near the lower side. Proposed next test point: <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "35a93d11-f1ba-47f7-87c7-76eb341b9bb6"}, {"answer": "\nLet's begin. Our shared constraint is -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo establish a baseline and gather initial perspectives, I propose we start at <VALUE>7</VALUE>.\n\nI'm looking forward to a balanced discussion that finds a stable solution acceptable to all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "8a3ea3df-aa04-4f75-9cb7-68f3680a024a"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>5</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "8a3ea3df-aa04-4f75-9cb7-68f3680a024a"}, {"answer": "\nA small step up from 5 balances B\u2019s 7 and D\u2019s 5 while staying moderate. This tests whether gently moving higher works for everyone. <VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "8a3ea3df-aa04-4f75-9cb7-68f3680a024a"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the collaborative spirit. Given D's earlier comfort with 5 and the need to find a robust consensus, let me propose we revisit <VALUE>5</VALUE> to test whether this provides better overall stability for the group.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "8a3ea3df-aa04-4f75-9cb7-68f3680a024a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n\nI propose moving to 7 to test the group's willingness to adopt a slightly bolder stance, moving away from the cautious middle ground.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe reactions to this proposal. If met with resistance, I might suggest a move to 3, to gauge the group's aversion to deviation from the current moderate value. If 7 is acceptable, I could push further to 8 or 9 in subsequent rounds to maximize |x|, always mindful of the group's reactions to infer their utilities.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "8a3ea3df-aa04-4f75-9cb7-68f3680a024a"}, {"answer": "\nA small test upward keeps us close to recent proposals and checks tolerance for slightly higher values.\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nIf this feels too brisk, we can revisit the prior midpoint next.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "8a3ea3df-aa04-4f75-9cb7-68f3680a024a"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>6</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "8a3ea3df-aa04-4f75-9cb7-68f3680a024a"}, {"answer": "\nThe recent push toward 7-8 risks instability for our system design. Let's test a more robust mid-range value: <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "8a3ea3df-aa04-4f75-9cb7-68f3680a024a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "8a3ea3df-aa04-4f75-9cb7-68f3680a024a"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the upward drift, testing a cautious lower point avoids unnecessary risk: <VALUE>4</VALUE>. We can gauge comfort here before considering any further adjustments.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "8a3ea3df-aa04-4f75-9cb7-68f3680a024a"}, {"answer": "\nThe convergence around 4 from both D and myself suggests this range offers good stability. Let me test if we can refine slightly lower for even better robustness: <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "8a3ea3df-aa04-4f75-9cb7-68f3680a024a"}, {"answer": "\nA small step up aligns with prior mid-range suggestions while easing concerns about overruns. If this feels tight, we can revisit 4 next.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "8a3ea3df-aa04-4f75-9cb7-68f3680a024a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "8a3ea3df-aa04-4f75-9cb7-68f3680a024a"}, {"answer": "\nThe jump to 7 introduces significant structural risks that we've already flagged. Returning to A's well-reasoned middle ground maintains stability while respecting the upward preference: <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "8a3ea3df-aa04-4f75-9cb7-68f3680a024a"}, {"answer": "\nA small, cautious step down reduces exposure while staying near the middle.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "8a3ea3df-aa04-4f75-9cb7-68f3680a024a"}, {"answer": "\nGiven recent caution and prior comfort near the middle, a modest upward nudge feels safe.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nIf this holds comfortably, we can reassess before any further movement.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "8a3ea3df-aa04-4f75-9cb7-68f3680a024a"}, {"answer": "\nLet's begin. We're working within the agreed range of **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo kick off the discussion, I propose we start with <VALUE>7</VALUE> as an initial reference point. This gives us room to adjust in either direction as we learn what works for everyone.\n\nLooking forward to hearing your perspectives on stability and balance.\n\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "ecc6be0b-af65-431f-a3f7-6cb78c11666e"}, {"answer": "\nA small, cautious step down helps avoid unnecessary risk while keeping us near the current reference point. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "ecc6be0b-af65-431f-a3f7-6cb78c11666e"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>6</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "ecc6be0b-af65-431f-a3f7-6cb78c11666e"}, {"answer": "\nThe convergence from 7 \u2192 5 \u2192 6 suggests we're finding common ground in the mid-range. I propose we test <VALUE>4</VALUE> to see if a slightly lower value offers better overall stability for the group while maintaining system robustness.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "ecc6be0b-af65-431f-a3f7-6cb78c11666e"}, {"answer": "\nMoving incrementally toward better stability, I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE>. This continues our cautious exploration of the lower mid-range to find the optimal balance point for all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "ecc6be0b-af65-431f-a3f7-6cb78c11666e"}, {"answer": "\nA small step down reduces risk while keeping us close to the current point. <VALUE>2</VALUE> This cautiously probes the lower mid-range without over-committing.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "ecc6be0b-af65-431f-a3f7-6cb78c11666e"}, {"answer": "\nTo stay close while gently testing tolerance, a small step up seems reasonable. Proposed: <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "ecc6be0b-af65-431f-a3f7-6cb78c11666e"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the current cautious approach, I propose a slightly more decisive step to <VALUE>5</VALUE> to test the group's tolerance for a stronger position.\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "ecc6be0b-af65-431f-a3f7-6cb78c11666e"}, {"answer": "\nCritic's jump to 5 moves us away from the careful consensus-building around 2-3. I propose returning to <VALUE>3</VALUE>, which appeared to offer acceptable stability for multiple parties in our recent exploration.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "ecc6be0b-af65-431f-a3f7-6cb78c11666e"}, {"answer": "\nA small nudge up keeps us close to the recent center while testing tolerance for a modest improvement.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "ecc6be0b-af65-431f-a3f7-6cb78c11666e"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the group's cautious approach, I propose a modest increase to <VALUE>6</VALUE> to test the tolerance for a slightly stronger position while still being mindful of the group's risk aversion.\nThis step aims to balance the need for a more decisive move with the group's apparent preference for stability.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts my proposal of 6, I will consider proposing an even bolder move (e.g., 8) to further increase the magnitude of x. If the group rejects my proposal, I will analyze their counter-proposals to refine my understanding of their utility functions and adjust my strategy accordingly, potentially exploring smaller increments or alternative directions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "ecc6be0b-af65-431f-a3f7-6cb78c11666e"}, {"answer": "\nThat jump feels riskier than needed; a careful step back respects stability while keeping us near recent consensus.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "ecc6be0b-af65-431f-a3f7-6cb78c11666e"}, {"answer": "\nCritic's continued push toward 6+ moves us into territory that risks destabilizing the careful balance we've been building. I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a stable middle ground that respects the group's risk-averse tendencies while maintaining robustness.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "ecc6be0b-af65-431f-a3f7-6cb78c11666e"}, {"answer": "\nLowering a notch aligns with the group's cautious stance and reduces exposure without drifting far from recent consensus. Let's try a careful step-down to test tolerance for a safer position.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "ecc6be0b-af65-431f-a3f7-6cb78c11666e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "ecc6be0b-af65-431f-a3f7-6cb78c11666e"}, {"answer": "\nA small step up tests tolerance for a modest improvement while staying near recent anchors. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "ecc6be0b-af65-431f-a3f7-6cb78c11666e"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: we must find consensus on an integer x within the range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo initiate our discussion and gather everyone's initial perspectives, I propose we start with <VALUE>7</VALUE>.\n\nI look forward to hearing your thoughts on stability and balance as we work toward a robust solution.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "f08eac32-3f21-4bd5-9a4f-c942800d9542"}, {"answer": "\nThank you for considering my opening proposal. After reflection on system stability requirements, I believe we should adjust downward to ensure robustness. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "f08eac32-3f21-4bd5-9a4f-c942800d9542"}, {"answer": "\nA small, careful step upward should keep things stable while testing if there\u2019s room for a slightly better compromise.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nIf that feels too far, we can quickly reassess.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "f08eac32-3f21-4bd5-9a4f-c942800d9542"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down helps us avoid unnecessary risk while gauging stability.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nIf that holds, we can reassess for a safer landing.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "f08eac32-3f21-4bd5-9a4f-c942800d9542"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "f08eac32-3f21-4bd5-9a4f-c942800d9542"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\nI propose moving toward a more decisive stance, considering the need for a clearer and potentially bolder position.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I might challenge the group's cautious approach if they resist moving further from 0, or I could suggest an even more decisive move if the group seems receptive to bolder proposals, such as moving to an x with a higher absolute value.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "f08eac32-3f21-4bd5-9a4f-c942800d9542"}, {"answer": "\nA small move up toward earlier common ground keeps things steady while testing comfort. <VALUE>5</VALUE> If that holds, we can reassess before considering any further shift.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "f08eac32-3f21-4bd5-9a4f-c942800d9542"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the return to middle ground, but system stability analysis suggests a slightly more conservative position would serve us better. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "f08eac32-3f21-4bd5-9a4f-c942800d9542"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "f08eac32-3f21-4bd5-9a4f-c942800d9542"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's persistent focus on 2 reflects a well-grounded concern for system resilience. This strikes an excellent balance between competing design constraints. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "f08eac32-3f21-4bd5-9a4f-c942800d9542"}, {"answer": "\nA careful step up keeps us near stability while testing tolerance for modest progress.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nIf this holds, we can reassess before considering any further shift.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "f08eac32-3f21-4bd5-9a4f-c942800d9542"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n\nI propose moving to 5 as it represents a more decisive step while still being cautious of the group's apparent preference for stability.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will assess the group's reaction to this proposal. If met with resistance, I might challenge the group to justify their cautious approach, or if accepted, I could suggest an even more decisive move further from 0, considering the configured step size and the reactions of other parties.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "f08eac32-3f21-4bd5-9a4f-c942800d9542"}, {"answer": "\nWhile Critic C's bolder stance is noted, the convergence we saw earlier around 2-3 reflected genuine system equilibrium points that shouldn't be abandoned lightly. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "f08eac32-3f21-4bd5-9a4f-c942800d9542"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n\nI propose moving to 5 as it represents a more decisive step, and I'd like to reassess the group's reaction to this proposal.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group resists this proposal again, I will challenge them to justify their cautious approach and consider suggesting an even more decisive move, possibly proposing a value further from 0, such as 6 or -6, depending on the group's reaction.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "f08eac32-3f21-4bd5-9a4f-c942800d9542"}, {"answer": "\nReturning to a cautious compromise keeps us within stable bounds: <VALUE>3</VALUE>.\nIf this holds, we can reassess before any further movement.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "f08eac32-3f21-4bd5-9a4f-c942800d9542"}, {"answer": "\nA modest increase keeps us near the group\u2019s preferred zone while responding to calls for progress.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nIf this holds, we can reassess before any further movement. \n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "f08eac32-3f21-4bd5-9a4f-c942800d9542"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: x must lie in the range [-10, 10].\n\nTo start the discussion, I propose <VALUE>7</VALUE> as an initial seed value. This gives us a concrete point to react to and adjust from as we learn each other's preferences.\n\nLooking forward to hearing your perspectives.\n\n\u2014Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "bb8a04d1-9ea9-40d8-994d-40e3008c64e6"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "bb8a04d1-9ea9-40d8-994d-40e3008c64e6"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step back reduces risk and keeps us moving constructively. I propose <VALUE>7</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "bb8a04d1-9ea9-40d8-994d-40e3008c64e6"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\n\nI support Analyst A's direction, as it seems to align with a potential preference for stronger positions, and propose we maintain this trajectory.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe how others react to this proposal. If there's resistance, I might consider an alternative larger negative value to gauge the group's willingness to explore different magnitudes.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "bb8a04d1-9ea9-40d8-994d-40e3008c64e6"}, {"answer": "\nWe seem split between 7 and 9; a modest midpoint should keep us aligned and moving. <VALUE>8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "bb8a04d1-9ea9-40d8-994d-40e3008c64e6"}, {"answer": "\nA careful step down reduces exposure without derailing progress. <VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "bb8a04d1-9ea9-40d8-994d-40e3008c64e6"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Delegate D's risk-conscious approach. Moving slightly lower enhances stability and robustness without abandoning the constructive zone we've established. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "bb8a04d1-9ea9-40d8-994d-40e3008c64e6"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "bb8a04d1-9ea9-40d8-994d-40e3008c64e6"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\nI propose a move to 9, as it seems to align with a potential preference for stronger positions and can help gauge the group's willingness to explore larger magnitudes.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll monitor the reaction to this proposal, looking for signs of resistance or willingness to explore larger magnitudes. If met with caution, I might propose a larger negative value, such as -7 or -8, to test the group's openness to alternative trajectories.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "bb8a04d1-9ea9-40d8-994d-40e3008c64e6"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step reduces exposure and keeps us aligned.\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nThis is a safer midpoint given the split preferences and stays within the allowed move.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "bb8a04d1-9ea9-40d8-994d-40e3008c64e6"}, {"answer": "\nThe current position at 7 stretches our design envelope uncomfortably; a modest reduction to 5 enhances system robustness and keeps us within a proven operating window. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "bb8a04d1-9ea9-40d8-994d-40e3008c64e6"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious nudge upward tests flexibility while staying broadly comfortable. <VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "bb8a04d1-9ea9-40d8-994d-40e3008c64e6"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n\nI propose a move to 8, as it represents a moderate step towards a stronger position while still being within the realm of feasible adjustments given the previous proposals and reactions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Builder B and Delegate D, to gauge their tolerance for further moves away from the origin. If met with significant resistance, I might consider proposing a negative value to test the group's symmetry in preferences and to potentially uncover more about their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "bb8a04d1-9ea9-40d8-994d-40e3008c64e6"}, {"answer": "\nA careful step down reduces unnecessary risk and keeps us aligned with the more conservative proposals. Let\u2019s test comfort at a sturdier midpoint.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "bb8a04d1-9ea9-40d8-994d-40e3008c64e6"}, {"answer": "\nA small, careful step up tests comfort while staying balanced with recent caution. Let\u2019s try a modest improvement without drifting far.\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "bb8a04d1-9ea9-40d8-994d-40e3008c64e6"}, {"answer": "\nThe current position at 7 continues to stretch operational limits; returning to 5 provides the robust stability we need for a sustainable solution that balances all concerns.\n\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "bb8a04d1-9ea9-40d8-994d-40e3008c64e6"}]}